# Exclude large binary files that should be downloaded
# Active now, and deliberately not scoped to roms/ the way the disks line
# below is scoped: that directory is gone and no ROM belongs anywhere in this
# tree.  roms/emu_avw.rom, roms/emu_romwbw.rom and roms/SBC_simh_std.rom were
# deleted on 2026-09-07, and the vcxproj (the Debug arm has no PostBuildEvent
# at all now; the Release one at z80cpmw.vcxproj:165-181 copies only the
# app-local CRT), build-msix.ps1 and the NSIS installer all stopped staging
# one, so no build of this application produces a roms directory any more.
# Every ROM comes from the romwbw_disks catalog and is checked against the
# size and the sha256 that only that catalog carries (DiskCatalog::verifyRom,
# at DiskCatalog.cpp:214) before it is loaded, so a ROM committed here could
# only be an unverifiable second copy going stale against what the catalog
# serves - which is what the two deleted emulator ROMs had become:
# byte-identical to each other and to the catalog's emu_avw-v0-3.5.1.rom,
# sha256 4b11402a29fad22de304775b7c415eb6a74600df06bd57828b9931a7e9693258,
# measured 2026-09-07.  The three names still appear in the uninstaller, to
# clean up installs that had them; nothing installs them any more.
*.rom

# Not a commented-out intention any more.  CLAUDE.md's standing rule is that
# every ROM and every disk image comes from the romwbw_disks catalog, reached
# through the one URL compiled in - the index at CatalogV0.cpp:24, there being
# no RELEASE_TAG in this tree any more - and that nothing is bundled in any
# package; disks/cpm_wbw.img and disks/zsys_wbw.img were the last two tracked
# here, they were what the deleted MainWindow::loadDefaultDisks() wanted, and no
# packaging script has staged them since dbd53b1.  This is what stops the next
# one being committed by accident.
disks/*.img

# Upstream repos (pulled for reference)
upstream/

# Test output artifacts
nul
dist/
